class_name Rigs
## Data for skeletal (cut-out mesh) characters. Coordinates are texture pixels of the
## character sprite. Each bone: [name, parent, joint x, joint y, tip x, tip y, greed, flags]
##   greed  - how strongly the bone claims nearby mesh vertices (distance divisor)
##   flags  - "j" = procedural jiggle (secondary motion), "n" = no skin weights (weapon socket)
## Clips: name -> {len, loop, keys: {"bone.rot"/"bone.pos"/"bone.scl"/"root.*": [[t, v], ...]}}
## rot = radians added to rest, pos = texture px offset, scl = [sx, sy]. Positive rot = clockwise.
## Converting another character = add an entry here (bones + clips) and list its id in SKELETAL.

const SKELETAL := ["goblin", "boss_lich"]   # enemy ids that use SkelActor; others stay on Actor

